main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ explicit-targ \+ deduced trailing pack instantiates: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG must FAIL: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
N5008 [temp.arg.explicit]/3, [temp.deduct.call]/3: a function template called
with an explicit leading template argument and a trailing parameter pack deduced
from the call arguments must instantiate with the pack bound to exactly the
supplied trailing arguments.  With a multi-element deduced pack (>= 2), the
instantiated candidate is built with one EXTRA pack parameter, so
disambiguate_functions rejects it on arity; resolution then bails via the
"all candidates are templates" SFINAE-tolerance path, discarding the enclosing
statement and verifying only vacuously.  A single-element deduced pack already
works.  This is the function-template analogue of
cpp11_partial_spec_pack_after_fixed and the root of multi-argument
std::function's _M_invoke/__invoke_r dispatch.  Flip to CORE once the
explicit-leading-arg + deduced-trailing-pack instantiation has the correct arity.
